6430-## 14. Entry-Local Anti-Pattern Interpretation Rule
6431-
6432-Each entry’s `anti_patterns` field only means:
6433-
6434-- it statically describes **which structural mistakes the example should avoid**
6435-- it does not perform runtime detection or scoring
6436-- it is warning metadata that may be referenced by a controller
6437-
6438----
6439-
6440-## 15. Generalization Rule
6441-
6442-### 15.1 Allowed generalization
6443-
6444-- preserve section names or lightly compress them
6445-- replace placeholders with current task/user context
6446-- adjust density within the same task family
6447-- specialize verification wording within the same verification pattern
6448-- reuse family-level structure for advanced prompting, multimodal, workflow, or evaluation artifacts without reusing content
6449-
6450-### 15.2 Not allowed
6451-
6452-- reusing factual content from an example body
6453-- transplanting domain facts from an example directly into the current task
6454-- adding selection rules that do not exist in the entry body
6455-- embedding cross-entry priority or scoring logic
6456-- converting a structure exemplar into runtime policy
6457-
6458----
6459-
6460-## 16. Compression Rule
6461-
6462-This catalog preserves data density but does not embed runtime policy.
6463-
6464-- More entries do not justify embedding selection logic
6465-- Richer explanation does not justify controller language
6466-- More advanced examples do not justify policy ownership shift
6467-- The catalog may become richer, but it may not gain decision authority
6468-
6469----
