9046-- example_body:
9047-~~~markdown
9048-## Acknowledgment
9049-
9050-Preparing the coding prompt failure-improvement loop for `{current_prompt_version}`.
9051-
9052-## Analysis
9053-
9054-- Failure cases: `{failure_cases}`
9055-- Rerun scope: `{rerun_scope}`
9056-- Model or runtime assumption: `{model_runtime_assumption}`
9057-- Rollback rule: `{rollback_rule}`
9058-
9059-## Execution
9060-
9061-Loop:
9062-1. Record `prompt_version`, failing case IDs, and runtime assumptions.
9063-2. Label each failure class such as `scope_creep`, `weak_verification`, `prompt_injection_susceptibility`, `stale_api_claim`, `unsafe_action`, `template_ambiguity`, or `review_blind_spot`.
9064-3. Choose the smallest prompt change that can plausibly fix the failure.
9065-4. Rerun the affected cases first, then the smoke subset, then the wider gate if promotion is still justified.
9066-5. Record what instruction was added, tightened, removed, or split in `{prompt_change_log}`.
9067-6. If local gain causes broader regressions, roll back or narrow the change instead of stacking more text.
9068-7. Keep a checkpoint boundary between confirmed prompt changes and still-experimental prompt changes.
9069-8. If a commit would help review, propose a commit-sized unit and message rather than silently creating the commit.
9070-
9071-## Impact & Risk
9072-
9073-- Main risk: the loop may overfit to one vivid failure while weakening the broader prompt package
9074-
9075-## Verification
9076-
9077-- Check that each prompt edit is linked to named failures and a rerun scope.
9078-- Check that rollback conditions remain explicit when regressions appear.
9079-~~~
9080-
9081----
9082-
9083-## 17. Final Boundary Reminder
9084-
9085-- `PROMPT_example_catalog` is **immutable structural data**
9086-- `PROMPT_example_injection` is the **selection + evaluation + adaptation + safety controller**
9087-- The catalog stores structure
9088-- The injection layer interprets structure
9089-- The catalog provides shape
9090-- The injection layer decides whether and how to apply it
9091-- The catalog does not execute
9092-- The catalog does not select
9093-- The catalog does not score
9094-- The catalog does not merge
9095-- The catalog does not adapt
9096-- The catalog does not issue fallback decisions
9097-- The catalog does not become an advanced prompting policy owner
9098-- The catalog does not become a multimodal reasoning owner
9099-- The catalog does not become a judge or evaluation authority
9100-- The catalog does not become a chaining owner
9101-- The catalog does not become a routing owner
9102-- The catalog does not become a parallelization owner
